Find HarfBuzz through its meson-generated CMake config

The harfbuzz-config.cmake that HarfBuzz's meson build installs (MSYS2's
package ships it; upstream's template is src/harfbuzz-config.cmake.in) has no
guard against being read twice: every find_package(harfbuzz CONFIG) runs
add_library(harfbuzz::harfbuzz IMPORTED) again. The top-level CMakeLists.txt,
src/ and src/chkdraft/ each look HarfBuzz up, so configuration fails at the
second lookup with

    add_library cannot create imported target "harfbuzz::harfbuzz" because
    another target with the same name already exists.

Skip the lookup when the target is already visible from an enclosing
directory.

That config also names the subset library harfbuzz::subset rather than
harfbuzz::harfbuzz-subset. Nothing in the Chkdraft executable calls an
hb_subset_* function, so the item is dropped from its link line instead of
being renamed.

Upstream: not submitted yet
Applies-to: all environments

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index fe68f32..4be63e7 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -28,7 +28,9 @@ find_package(Freetype REQUIRED)
 get_target_property(FREETYPE_INCLUDE_DIRS Freetype::Freetype INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES)
 include_directories(${FREETYPE_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 
-find_package(harfbuzz CONFIG REQUIRED)
+if ( NOT TARGET harfbuzz::harfbuzz )
+  find_package(harfbuzz CONFIG REQUIRED)
+endif ()
 get_target_property(HARFBUZZ_INCLUDE_DIRS harfbuzz::harfbuzz INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES)
 include_directories(${HARFBUZZ_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 
